    STATUS_COMPACT_BELOW = "Compact minimap: in Edit Mode the box is below the minimap – then ezMap changes nothing, Blizzard's layout stays.",
    OPT_minimapCompact = "Compact minimap (box below, coordinates in it)",
    OPT_minimapCompact_TIP = "What you get: Blizzard's box with zone name, coordinates and clock (\"Auberdine 38.6, 43.0 18:07\") sits at the bottom edge of the ring, and the minimap moves up into its place. The magnifier (tracking) and the calendar sit round like Blizzard's buttons on the ring, the addon compartment right of the calendar. The box gets a little wider for the coordinates; whether they show is still Blizzard's setting. With ezPanel: turning it on moves its \"Location\" and \"Clock\" blocks to the right of the bar, and while both are there, Blizzard's box is hidden. Only while the box is above the minimap in Edit Mode; changes only after combat. With ezPanel: if its \"Reserve space at the top\" is off, the minimap only moves up to just below the bar. Off: everything back in Blizzard's place. If SexyMap is running, it styles the minimap.",
    OPT_minimapSquare = "Square minimap (more area)",
    OPT_minimapSquare_TIP = "What you get: the game doesn't zoom out further than level 0, but the minimap is really a square – Blizzard's round mask cuts off the corners. Square, you see about 27% more area at the same level. Blizzard's round frame is replaced by a plain one; position and size stay. Changes only after combat. If SexyMap is running, it styles the minimap.",
    STATUS_ZOOM = "Minimap: %s Zoom out by itself: off.",
    STATUS_ZOOM_AUTO = "Minimap: %s Zooms out by itself after %d |4second:seconds;.",
    STATUS_ZOOM_OTHER = "Minimap: %s %s zooms out by itself, so ezMap doesn't.",
    OPT_HEADER_MINIMAP = "Minimap",
    OPT_HEADER_MINIMAP_TIP = "The game doesn't zoom out further than level 0 (mouse wheel or Blizzard's minus all the way). Making it bigger only shows the same area larger; the square minimap adds the corners. Destinations for the map pin are in the minimap's tracking menu.",
    OPT_minimapAutoZoomDelay = "Zoom back out by itself",
    OPT_minimapAutoZoomDelay_TIP = "What you get: after zooming in (mouse wheel, plus) the minimap jumps back to the widest level after this many seconds. All the way left (\"off\") it stays as you zoomed it (default). If the mouse is still on the minimap, ezMap waits. If another addon already does this (e.g. SexyMap), ezMap stays out of the way. The same switch is a tick in the minimap's tracking menu; it remembers the last time you chose.",

    OPT_ENTER = "Set a waypoint",
    OPT_ENTER_BUTTON = "Coordinates",
    OPT_ENTER_TIP = "Opens an input box for coordinates in your zone (like /way). A zone name may come first and a name for the pin after.",
    OPT_HEADER_WAY = "Waypoints",
    OPT_wayTrack = "Turn on navigation",
    OPT_wayTrack_TIP = "Off by default because it changes Blizzard's navigation without your click. On: when ezMap sets a map pin, Blizzard's arrow and distance at the edge of the screen guide you there without clicking it on the map first – also when a gathering route or ezQuest's levelling route moves on. In combat ezMap only sets the pin; the arrow follows afterwards. Off: ezMap only sets the pin; click the pin on Blizzard's world map to turn on the arrow.",
    OPTIN_wayTrack = "Turns on Blizzard's navigation (arrow and distance) without a click whenever ezMap sets a map pin – also when a gathering route or ezQuest's levelling route moves on. Without the switch ezMap only sets the pin; a click on the pin on the world map turns on the arrow.",
    OPT_waySlash = "Command /way",
    OPT_waySlash_TIP = "What you get: waypoints from guides and comments (/way 45.3 32.1) become Blizzard's map pin right away. If another addon (e.g. TomTom) already has /way, it keeps it and ezMap uses /ezway. Takes effect after /reload.",
    OPT_wayAutoClear = "Remove pin on arrival",
    OPT_wayAutoClear_TIP = "What you get: when you reach Blizzard's map pin, it disappears together with the arrow after 3 or 5 seconds – no matter who set it (/way, map menu, Ctrl-click, trainers, gathering spots). \"Off\": the pin stays until you remove it yourself. If you walk away first (farther than 20 yards), it stays. Arrival means: within 10 yards after having been farther away – so a pin on your own spot (/way here) stays while you are there; if you come back later, it disappears like any other. The pin of a route you follow always stays. Without a map position (some instances) ezMap removes nothing. Source: Blizzard's \"destination reached\" or your position as reported by the game.",
    OPT_HERE = "My position",
    OPT_HERE_BUTTON = "Pin",
    OPT_HERE_TIP = "Puts the map pin where you stand right now – to find the spot again or to share it as a link.",
    OPT_CLEAR = "Map pin",
    OPT_CLEAR_BUTTON = "Remove",
    OPT_CLEAR_TIP = "Removes Blizzard's map pin (like /way clear).",
    OPT_HEADER_FLIGHTS = "Flight times",
    OPT_flightTimes = "Flight time in the tooltip",
    OPT_flightTimes_TIP = "What you get: the flight map tells you how long a flight takes before you take off. ezMap learns every route on its first flight; until then it says \"not known yet\". If Leatrix Plus or InFlight already shows flight times, ezMap stays out of the way.",
    OPT_flightBar = "Bar during the flight",
    OPT_flightBar_TIP = "What you get: you know when you'll arrive. A bar in the style of Blizzard's cast bar shows destination and time left (top centre by default, docked below Blizzard's breath bar; movable in Edit Mode or with \"Move parts\" under General); the cross next to it (or a right-click) hides it for this flight.",
    OPT_PREVIEW = "Preview",
    OPT_PREVIEW_BUTTON = "Show",
    OPT_PREVIEW_TIP = "Shows the flight bar for ten seconds with an example route.",
    OPT_FLIGHT_LIST = "Learned flight times",
    OPT_FLIGHT_LIST_TIP = "Prints every learned route with its duration to chat (like /ezmap flight).",
    OPT_LIST_BUTTON = "List",
    OPT_HEADER_TRAINERS = "Trainers",
    OPT_TRAINER_LIST = "Remembered trainers",
    OPT_TRAINER_LIST_TIP = "Prints every remembered trainer with location to chat (like /ezmap trainers).",
    OPT_STATUS_TIP = "Shows which command sets waypoints, how many flight times and trainers ezMap knows and which other addon it leaves the job to (TomTom, Leatrix Plus, InFlight, Questie, Forever Tweaks, Leatrix Maps).",
    OPT_FLIGHT_RESET = "Forget flight times",
    OPT_FLIGHT_RESET_TIP = "Deletes all learned flight times (asks first) – in ezCore's shared database, which other ezCollection modules read as well. ezMap learns them again while flying.",
    OPT_TRAINER_FORGET = "Forget trainers",
    OPT_TRAINER_FORGET_TIP = "Forgets all remembered trainers (asks first) – in ezCore's shared NPC knowledge, so for all ez modules. Vendors stay.",
